Here's one way to implement it:  

```python
def abbrev_num(x):
    if x < 1000:
        return str(x)
    elif x < 1_000_000:
        val = round(x / 1000)
        if val >= 100:
            return f"{val}K"
        return f"{x // 1000}.{ (x % 1000) // 100 }K"
    else:
        val = round(x / 1_000_000)
        if val >= 100:
            return f"{val}M"
        return f"{x // 1_000_000}.{ (x % 1_000_000) // 100_000 }M"
``` [end of text]


